    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The excerpts show no meaningful contextual differences in policy debate.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_e564c7c418a42d7e\",\"quote\":\"These amendment orders relate to the Heavy Commercial Vehicles in Kent (No. 1) Order 2019 and the Heavy Commercial Vehicles in Kent (No. 2) Order 2019. Although the Heavy Commercial Vehicles in Kent (No. 3) (Amendment) Order 2020 is subject to the negative procedure, the House should be aware of it when considering the other two amending orders. Together they support the effective…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_61805ccc06c4d0a2\",\"quote\":\"Under the Environment Bill, we will have a 25-year environment improvement plan that addresses issues such as air quality. There will also be targets set for air quality under the Bill.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"absence of any discussion of the Kent-specific context of Operation Brock and related policy debates.\",\"mechanism\":\"The excerpts present distinct policy debates (Operation Brock, Environment Bill) without acknowledging their potential contextual differences.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim ignores the specific operational and policy contexts driving the debates, leading to a misleading impression of similarity.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The excerpts do not explicitly state a lack of contextual differences; they simply present different policy discussions. This does not negate the possibility of contextual distinctions.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The excerpts detail separate policy debates – Operation Brock and the Environment Bill – failing to acknowledge potential contextual differences in their framing and implications. This constitutes a significant contextual flattening.\"}",
